.SH NAME
\fBplease\fR \- An AI-native git CLI. You never type raw git commands.

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B please
.RI "<command> " [ args... ]
.br
.B please
.RI """<what you want to do>"""

.SH DESCRIPTION
Welcome to the future of version control.
.PP
\fBplease\fR is an AI-native interface to Git. Git remains the robust engine underneath, but \fBplease\fR takes over the steering wheel. Instead of wrestling with arcane flags, detached heads, and forgotten commit messages, you simply tell the CLI what you want.
.PP
Powered by Anthropic Claude, Google Gemini, or OpenAI ChatGPT, it handles the tedious parts—staging, summarizing diffs, and formatting commits—while leaving the heavy lifting to Git.
.PP
\fBDev-Friendly Features:\fR
.IP \[bu] 2
\fBFuzzy Matching:\fR Typoed `swich` or `brnach`? \fBplease\fR fixes it on the fly. No more "command not found".
.IP \[bu]
\fBZero-Jargon Status:\fR `please status` tells you exactly what's going on in plain English.
.IP \[bu]
\fBAuto-Guardrails:\fR Prevents accidentally committing secrets (`.env`) or massive junk directories (`node_modules`) unless explicitly forced.

.SH COMMANDS

.SS "Core Workflow"
.TP
.B please commit
Analyzes your working tree, skips secrets/junk, stages changes, and uses AI to split your work into logically coherent, beautifully written commits.
.TP
.B please push
Runs \fBplease commit\fR, then pushes to origin. Automatically sets up the upstream tracking branch if it's your first push.
.TP
.B please sync [exactly]
The ultimate pull command. Fetches and merges the upstream. If you add \fBexactly\fR, it aggressively destroys local deviations to perfectly mirror the remote (destructive, requires confirmation).

.SS "Branch Management"
.TP
.B please branch \fI[name]\fR
Lists branches. If a name is provided, creates and immediately switches to it.
.TP
.B please switch \fI<name>\fR
Fuzzy-switches to a branch. Offers to create it if missing.
.TP
.B please rename \fI<new-name>\fR
Renames the current branch locally \fIand\fR on the remote simultaneously.
.TP
.B please cleanup
Sweeps away local branches that have already been merged into main.

.SS "Oh Sh*t / Recovery"
.TP
.B please undo
Soft-resets the last commit, leaving your files intact so you can fix your mistakes.
.TP
.B please redo
Brings back the undone commit (provided history hasn't diverged).
.TP
.B please discard
Nukes all uncommitted changes from orbit. (Requires confirmation).
.TP
.B please move-commit \fI<branch>\fR
Committed to main by accident? This rips your last commit off and moves it to the specified branch in one motion.
.TP
.B please purge \fI<path>\fR
Leaked a private key? This uses filter-repo/filter-branch to violently scrub a file from your entire git history.

.SS "History & State"
.TP
.B please status
A sane, readable view of your repository state.
.TP
.B please log
A gorgeous, terminal-optimized commit graph.
.TP
.B please squash \fI[n | ref]\fR
Squashes commits into one, complete with an AI-generated summary message.
.TP
.B please stash \fI[list | pop | drop]\fR
Stashes all changes (including untracked files).

.SS "AI Agent Mode"
.TP
.B please \fI"write me a commit and open a PR"\fR
Natural language fallback. If it's not a standard command, the AI figures out the raw Git/CLI commands needed to achieve your goal and executes them on your behalf.
.TP
.B please chat
Starts a persistent, multi-turn conversational session with the AI agent.

.SH EXAMPLES

.B 1. Committing without thinking:
.EX
$ please commit
.EE
.I (The AI stages files, writes the message, and commits.)

.B 2. Fixing a typo in the branch name:
.EX
$ please rename feature/new-ui
.EE

.B 3. Getting unstuck using the Agent:
.EX
$ please "I accidentally deleted my src folder, help me get it back"
.EE

.B 4. Accessing detailed in-app documentation:
.EX
$ please man commit
$ please push --help
.EE

.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B PLEASE_API_KEY
Overrides the globally configured API key for the AI provider.
.TP
.B PLEASE_PROVIDER
Overrides the configured provider (anthropic, google, openai).

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.please/config
Global JSON configuration holding provider preferences and encrypted keys.
.TP
.I .git/PLEASE.MD
Local repository context. The AI reads this to understand your codebase's vibe.

.SH EXIT STATUS
\fB0\fR   Success. All operations completed cleanly.
.br
\fB1\fR   General error (network failure, bad configuration, or Git rejection).
.br
\fB130\fR Operation cancelled by the user (Ctrl+C or 'no' on a destructive prompt).

